{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>As it is removed, etc.</b> Rashi explained: regarding the slaughter of consecrated offerings, Scripture requires learning from it that in consecrated offerings one does not derive a learning from a learning. The explanation: Scripture needs to spell out the lifting up of the emurim of the bull of the anointed priest in order to learn from it the lifting up of the emurim of the bull of a communal sin-offering of inadvertency, as it is written further on, ״ועשה לפר העלם של צבור כאשר עשה לפר החטאת של כהן משיח״ (and he shall do to the bull of the communal inadvertency as he did to the bull of the sin-offering of the anointed priest). And if it had not spelled out for you here the lifting up of the emurim of the bull of the anointed priest, how would the verse of ״ועשה לפר״ etc. come to derive the lifting up of the emurim of the bull of a communal inadvertency from the lifting up of the emurim of the bull of the anointed priest — when the lifting up of the emurim of the bull of the anointed priest itself would need to be derived from the lifting up of the emurim of the ox of well-being offerings, and one does not derive a learning from a learning in consecrated offerings?" "<b>As it is removed from the ox of the sacrifice of well-being offerings.</b> To teach that communal well-being offerings are brought as the well-being offering of an ox. And well-being offerings of a lamb do not push aside Shabbat and impurity, like communal well-being offerings."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:59.909849580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}